Follow-up to #91, which made `karr list --sort priority` read the config list backwards so the most urgent task opens the list, agreeing with what `karr pick` hands out. At the time that direction disagreed with kanban-md, so it was written up as a deliberate deviation.

kanban-md has since taken the same change: commit c783157 "fix: sort priority lists highest first" (upstream main, reference checkout now at that commit). It solves it one layer up rather than in the comparator -- `cmd/list.go` flips `reverse` when the sort key is `priority`, leaving `internal/board/sort.go` ascending -- but the observable behaviour is now identical to karrs: `--sort priority` opens with the most urgent task, `--reverse` gives the least-urgent-first view. Their e2e coverage pins both directions, and their README documents it the same way.

So the deviation is gone and only the prose claiming it is left. Stale wording, each verified against the tree:

- lib/App/karr/Cmd/List.pm:74-77 (POD) -- "This direction is a documented deviation from kanban-md, whose ascending config order opens the list with the least urgent task -- the opposite of its own pick."
- lib/App/karr/Cmd/List.pm:270 (comment above _comparators) -- "kanban-md ascending order (sort.go:29) put the least urgent task on top, the exact opposite of pick." Reads as a live divergence in context, even though the verb is past tense. Note sort.go:29 is still accurate as a description of their comparator; what changed sits in cmd/list.go.
- Changes:129-130 -- "This deliberately deviates from kanban-md, whose `list --sort priority` still follows the config order ascending."

No behaviour change: karr already does the right thing and keeps its own implementation (the comparator reads the list backwards; kanban-md flips the reverse flag). Only the claim of divergence is wrong. Worth keeping in the wording: karr breaks ties on id, which kanban-md does not, so identical-priority ordering is still karrs own.

Decided with the maintainer while this was found: the default sort of `karr list` stays `id`. This ticket is about the `--sort priority` direction only.
Landed on main as a9ec82a (combined commit with the other three tickets). Full suite green over the combined tree: 112 files, 756 tests.
